hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16728","He said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Amr ibn Muadh al-Ashhali, from his grandmother, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O believing women, let none of you despise for her neighbor even a burnt sheep hoof."
"27614","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, he said: Haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, he said: Haddathana Musa ibn Wardan, he said: Ubayd ibn Hunayn, freedman of Kharijah, informed me that the woman who asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about fasting Saturday narrated to him that she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that, and he said: Neither for you nor against you."
"27910","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Daylam Abu Ghalib al-Qattan narrated to me, he said: al-Hakam ibn Jahl narrated to me, he said: Umm al-Kiram narrated to me that she performed Hajj. She said: I met a woman at Makkah with many attendants, and upon none of them was jewelry except silver. I said to her: Why do I see upon none of your attendants jewelry except silver. She said: My grandfather was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I was with him, wearing two gold earrings, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two brands of fire. So we, the people of the house, none of us wears jewelry except silver."
"28001","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, narrated Mamar, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, that a woman narrated to him, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept then woke while laughing, so I said: Are you laughing at me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but at people from my ummah who go out as warriors in the sea, their example being like kings on couches. She said: Then he slept then woke again laughing, so I said: Are you laughing at me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but at people from my ummah who go out as warriors in the sea and return with little spoils, forgiven. She said: Supplicate Allah to make me among them, so he supplicated for her. He said: Ata ibn Yasar informed me, he said: So I saw her in an expedition led by Al-Mundhir ibn Az-Zubayr to the land of the Romans, she was with us, and she died in the land of the Romans."
"28010","Narrated Abdur-Razzaq, informed Mamar, from Wasil, freedman of Abi Uyaynah, from Musa ibn Ubayd, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, that a woman informed her that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between As-Safa and Al-Marwah saying: Sai is prescribed upon you, so perform sai."
"28011","Narrated Yazid ibn Harun, informed Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Damrah ibn Said, from his grandmother, from a woman of their women, she had prayed both qiblas with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and said: Dye with henna, one of you leaves dyeing until her hand becomes like the hand of a man. She said: So she did not leave dyeing until she met Allah Almighty, and she used to dye though she was eighty years old."
